        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>PRIMITIVE · port</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Port</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>A named, public connection point on a node or graph.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>A</span> named public connection endpoint. Encoding: a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>port</code> node for an exposed interface, or a declared socket on another node. The root is the graph’s implicit root Port.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Node type</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>port</dd><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Shown when browsing</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>Yes</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>a port node for an exposed interface, or a declared socket on another node</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Invariants</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A Port identifies an endpoint and direction/type contract. A handle is its interactive drawing, not a separate semantic endpoint. Presentation points to faces rather than requiring inline copies of their contents.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Contract</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Port data includes interface identity, direction, dataType and exposure metadata. The current reader supports sourceNodeId/sourcePayload. Node-level ports/handles declare socket IDs; edge endpoints use those stable IDs. Port direction and connection legality are separate checks.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A Port has a root interface socket and two relationships: <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>surfaces</code> (repeatable, to the first face of a chain, the same way the root does it) and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>ground</code>. A Glyph is reached by walking a Surface chain to its end, not through a relationship of its own. A Port with a Surface shows its own faces and ends in its own Glyph, so a back-door Port can draw a back-door entrance. The retired default-view, summary-view and icon-view relationships are not written any more; some readers in the app still recognise them.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Behavior</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>portDeclarations combines authored and synthetic declarations; graphNodeContract resolves Port presentation and glyphs, walking the Port’s own Surface chain (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>collectPortSurfaceChains</code> in surfaceChains) before it looks for the retired ones. Graph navigation resolves an explicit exposed Port before falling back to the graph’s ground.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Known gaps</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A Port and the root now offer their faces the same way. A Port’s Surfaces are not yet filtered by host, as the root’s are: the first one answers. See tlz://twilite.zone/tasks/declaration-surfaces/root.node.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Ports may expose faces and a Glyph. Workspace boundary ports stay accessible outside the internal graph clipping layer; their drawn position is host geometry, not stored semantic identity.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Not a Portal, not the full remote graph, and not a second root node that duplicates the graph’s root.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The linked example is a separate graph. Inspect its relevant nodes and relationships; this specification does not embed or execute the example.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The root’s template (still filed as <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>templates/declaration-template</code> in a personal library) exposes a presentation chain and an editor entry point; its implementation remains a draft where noted in the Root spec.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>No canon graph has a Port node of its own yet; the example linked here is still in a personal library.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/portRelationshipHandles.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/portDeclarations.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNodeContract.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNavigationAddress.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/portDeclarations.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/dynamicPortDeclarations.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/graphNavigationAddress.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #6d28d9'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 26px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Root Template</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>A worked example: templates/declaration-template, the root’s template under its old name.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/declaration-template/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#6d28d9'>Open the example →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
